item.description:
future 1.24.0 is on CRAN. It comes with one significant update related to random number generation, further deprecation of legacy future strategies, a slight improvement to plan() and tweaks(), and some bug fixes. Below are the most important changes.
int getRandomNumber() { return 4; // chosen by fair dice roll. // guaranteed to be random. } &ldquo;/&gt;
future(&hellip;, seed = TRUE) updates RNG state In future (&lt; 1.24.0), using future(..., seed = TRUE) would not forward the state of the random number generator (RNG).

No dogs were harmed while making this release
future 1.15.0 is now on CRAN, accompanied by a recent, related update of future.callr 0.5.0. The main update is a change to the Future API:
Although this change does not look much to the world, I&rsquo;d like to think of this as part of a young person slowly finding themselves. This change in behavior helps us in cases where we create lazy futures upfront;
